From: Sayantan Roychowdhury <sayantan.rc@e.email>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:17:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Issue 1776: Default to phone-only if no account

[a17: ContactEditorAccountsChangedActivity was removed; the editor now opens
Settings' "set default account" screen. Re-implemented in
ContactEditorFragment.selectAccountAndCreateContact(): when the only
writable account is the device one, create a phone-only contact directly.]

(cherry picked from commit 948becd76bd250fe3dfcb948fc4fd75fde954e26)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0127aPbuxQvhzD8TVw5auGLR
---
 .../android/contacts/editor/ContactEditorFragment.java    | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/contacts/editor/ContactEditorFragment.java b/src/com/android/contacts/editor/ContactEditorFragment.java
index d7d164f0a..ad4d1b0e8 100755
--- a/src/com/android/contacts/editor/ContactEditorFragment.java
+++ b/src/com/android/contacts/editor/ContactEditorFragment.java
@@ -1071,6 +1071,14 @@ public class ContactEditorFragment extends Fragment
         // If there is no default account or the accounts have changed such that we need to
         // prompt the user again, then launch the account prompt.
         if (mEditorUtils.shouldShowAccountChangedNotification(accounts)) {
+            // If the only writable account is the device one, default to a phone-only contact
+            // instead of asking the user to pick a default account.
+            final AccountWithDataSet localAccount = AccountWithDataSet.getLocalAccount(mContext);
+            if (accounts.isEmpty()
+                    || (accounts.size() == 1 && accounts.get(0).equals(localAccount))) {
+                createContact(localAccount);
+                return;
+            }
             Intent intent = new Intent(Settings.ACTION_SET_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT);
             // Prevent a second instance from being started on rotates
             intent.setFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TOP | Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_SINGLE_TOP);
